      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="vs">
      <div class="no"><h3><i class="ph-duotone ph-x-circle" style="color:var(--err)"></i>Hibernate on its own</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-x"></i><span>Java classes or XML for every entity</span></li>
          <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-x"></i><span>Values must already be the right Java type</span></li>
          <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-x"></i><span>Case-sensitive HQL names</span></li>
          <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-x"></i><span>Stack traces in Hibernate's terms</span></li>
          <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-x"></i><span>Its own transactions and its own cache</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="yes"><h3><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle" style="color:var(--accent)"></i>Hibernate through BxORM</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check"></i><span>A BoxLang class; mappings are generated in memory</span></li>
          <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check"></i><span><code>"42"</code>, dates and booleans converted for you</span></li>
          <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check"></i><span>Write HQL in any case, like the rest of BoxLang</span></li>
          <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check"></i><span><code>orm.*</code> errors with your names and the fix</span></li>
          <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check"></i><span>BoxLang's <code>transaction{}</code> and BoxCache</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 3. STATIC HELPERS -->
<section class="tint">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Static helpers</span>
      <h2>Every entity is <span class="grad">its own repository</span>.</h2>
      <p>No service objects, no base class, no injection. At startup every entity class gets static methods, and each one is the BIF you already know with the entity name filled in: same session, same events, same errors.</p>
      <div class="mgroups" style="margin-top:22px">
        <div class="mg"><b>Load</b><div><code>get()</code><code>getOrFail()</code><code>getAll()</code><code>read()</code><code>getReference()</code></div></div>
        <div class="mg"><b>Find</b><div><code>findWhere()</code><code>findAllWhere()</code><code>first()</code><code>exists()</code><code>count()</code><code>list()</code></div></div>
        <div class="mg"><b>Create and update</b><div><code>new()</code><code>firstOrNew()</code><code>firstOrCreate()</code><code>updateWhere()</code></div></div>
        <div class="mg"><b>Delete</b><div><code>deleteWhere()</code><code>criteria().deleteAll()</code><code>entityDelete( entity )</code></div><small><code>deleteWhere()</code> runs one <code>DELETE</code> and refuses an empty filter. <code>entityDelete()</code> fires events and honors soft delete.</small></div>
        <div class="mg"><b>Query</b><div><code>criteria()</code><code>executeQuery()</code></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="stage">
      <div class="stage-bar"><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="file">handlers/Orders.bx</span></div>
<pre class="code"><span class="k">function</span> <span class="f">show</span>( event, rc, prc ){
    <span class="c">// orm.notFound with a clear message if it's not there</span>
    prc.order = Order::<span class="f">getOrFail</span>( rc.id );
}

<span class="k">function</span> <span class="f">index</span>( event, rc, prc ){
    prc.orders = Order::<span class="f">list</span>( {
        max    : <span class="n">25</span>,
        offset : ( rc.page - <span class="n">1</span> ) * <span class="n">25</span>,
        sort   : <span class="s">"createdDate desc"</span>
    } );
    prc.total = Order::<span class="f">count</span>( { status : <span class="s">"open"</span> } );
}

<span class="k">function</span> <span class="f">tag</span>( event, rc, prc ){
    <span class="c">// find it, or create it on first use</span>
    <span class="k">return</span> Tag::<span class="f">firstOrCreate</span>( { name : rc.tag } );
}</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 4. CRITERIA -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap split rev">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Criteria queries</span>
      <h2>Queries that read like <span class="grad">sentences</span>.</h2>
      <p><code>entityCriteria()</code> builds a query one method at a time. Property names are checked as you go, values are always bound as parameters, and a dotted path joins its associations for you.</p>
      <ul class="checks">
        <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle"></i><span>Automatic joins from paths like <code>manufacturer.name</code></span></li>
        <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle"></i><span><code>anyOf()</code>, <code>allOf()</code>, subqueries, projections and grouping</span></li>
        <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle"></i><span><code>paginate()</code>, streaming, and bulk <code>updateAll()</code> / <code>deleteAll()</code></span></li>
        <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle"></i><span><code>asStruct()</code> builds JSON-ready structs without loading entities</span></li>
        <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle"></i><span>cborm's method names, so cborm code reads the same</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="stage">
        <div class="stage-bar"><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="file">inventory.bxs</span></div>
<pre class="code">cars = <span class="f">entityCriteria</span>( <span class="s">"Vehicle"</span> )
    .<span class="f">isEq</span>( <span class="s">"manufacturer.name"</span>, <span class="s">"Ford Motor Company"</span> )
    .<span class="f">isGt</span>( <span class="s">"year"</span>, <span class="n">2020</span> )
    .<span class="f">order</span>( <span class="s">"price"</span> )
    .<span class="f">list</span>();</pre>
      </div>
      <div class="erd">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 520 150" role="img" aria-label="Vehicle joined to Manufacturer through the manufacturer path">
          <defs><linearGradient id="lg" x1="0" x2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="##2ee66b"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="##00b8e6"/></linearGradient></defs>
          <g font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="12">
            <rect x="10" y="20" width="170" height="112" rx="12" fill="none" stroke="url(##lg)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="26" y="44" fill="##2ee66b" font-weight="600">Vehicle</text>
            <line x1="10" y1="54" x2="180" y2="54" stroke="rgba(141,184,168,.3)"/>
            <text x="26" y="74" fill="##8db8a8">year</text><text x="26" y="94" fill="##8db8a8">price</text><text x="26" y="114" fill="##e5f8ef">manufacturer ●</text>
            <rect x="340" y="20" width="170" height="92" rx="12" fill="none" stroke="url(##lg)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="356" y="44" fill="##2ee66b" font-weight="600">Manufacturer</text>
            <line x1="340" y1="54" x2="510" y2="54" stroke="rgba(141,184,168,.3)"/>
            <text x="356" y="74" fill="##e5f8ef">name ●</text><text x="356" y="94" fill="##8db8a8">country</text>
            <path d="M180 110 C 260 110, 260 70, 340 70" fill="none" stroke="url(##lg)" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 5"><animate attributeName="stroke-dashoffset" from="22" to="0" dur="1.2s" repeatCount="indefinite"/></path>
            <rect x="200" y="122" width="120" height="22" rx="11" fill="rgba(46,230,107,.12)" stroke="rgba(46,230,107,.4)"/>
            <text x="260" y="137" fill="##2ee66b" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11">inner join, by BxORM</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <div class="cap"><span><i class="ph-duotone ph-git-merge"></i>Same path joined once and reused</span><span><i class="ph-duotone ph-arrow-bend-down-right"></i>Left joins inside <code>anyOf()</code> and for ordering</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 5. NO CASTING -->
<section class="tint">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">No casting</span>
      <h2>BoxLang types in. <span class="grad">BoxLang types out.</span></h2>
      <p>BoxLang is dynamic; JDBC is not. BxORM puts a converter on every property, chosen from its <code>ormtype</code>, and uses BoxLang's own casters both ways. The string from your form is stored as an integer, and a date comes back as a BoxLang date.</p>
      <ul class="checks">
        <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle"></i><span><code>isEq( "id", "42" )</code> works for a numeric id</span></li>
        <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle"></i><span>A value that can't fit its column is an <code>orm.property.type</code> error, not a database surprise</span></li>
        <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle"></i><span>HQL names resolve case-insensitively, then the corrected query is cached</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="flow">
        <div class="frow h"><span>Your value</span><span></span><span>Converter</span><span></span><span>Column</span><span></span><span>You get back</span></div>
        <div class="frow"><code>rc.id = <span class="s">"42"</span></code><span class="arr">→</span><span class="conv">IntegerConverter</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="col2">INTEGER</span><span class="arr">→</span><code><span class="n">42</span></code></div>
        <div class="frow"><code>price = <span class="s">"19.99"</span></code><span class="arr">→</span><span class="conv">BigDecimalConverter</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="col2">DECIMAL</span><span class="arr">→</span><code><span class="n">19.99</span></code></div>
        <div class="frow"><code>created = <span class="f">now</span>()</code><span class="arr">→</span><span class="conv">DateTimeConverter</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="col2">TIMESTAMP</span><span class="arr">→</span><code>DateTime</code></div>
        <div class="frow"><code>active = <span class="k">true</span></code><span class="arr">→</span><span class="conv">BooleanConverter</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="col2">BOOLEAN</span><span class="arr">→</span><code><span class="k">true</span></code></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hql">
        <div class="line"><span class="bad">"from user where firstname = ?"</span><span class="good">→</span><span class="good">User.firstName</span></div>
        <small>Hibernate 6 and later resolve HQL names case-sensitively. BoxLang doesn't, so BxORM resolves them for you.</small>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 6. ERRORS -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap split rev">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Errors for humans</span>
      <h2>Errors that tell you <span class="grad">what to do next</span>.</h2>
      <p>Every error BxORM raises is written for BoxLang developers: the message uses your entity and property names, the detail says how to fix it, and misspelled names get a suggestion. All the context is in <code>extendedInfo</code>.</p>
      <ul class="checks">
        <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle"></i><span>Typed <code>orm.*</code> errors: catch one, a family, or all of them</span></li>
        <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle"></i><span>The HQL, parameters, generated SQL and constraint name, when you need them</span></li>
        <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle"></i><span><code>ormDiagnostics()</code> never throws and shows the ORM's state</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="term">
        <div class="stage-bar"><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="file">orm.property.unknown</span></div>
        <div class="anat">
          <div class="part"><span class="lbl">message</span><span class="msg"><span class="e">Manufacturer has no property [nmae].</span><br><span class="sug">Did you mean [name]?</span></span></div>
          <div class="part"><span class="lbl">detail</span><span>Properties: id, name, address, vehicles</span></div>
          <div class="part"><span class="lbl">extendedInfo</span><span><span class="c">{</span> hql : <span class="s">"from Manufacturer where nmae = 'x'"</span>, ... <span class="c">}</span></span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tree">
<div><span class="k">catch</span>( <span class="s">"orm.constraint.unique"</span> e ){ ... }</div>
<div style="height:10px"></div>
<div class="t0">orm</div>
<div><span class="br">├─ </span>orm.entity.notFound<em>Did you mean [User]?</em></div>
<div><span class="br">├─ </span>orm.property.unknown</div>
<div><span class="br">├─ </span>orm.query<span class="br">.*</span><em>syntax, semantic, parameter, nonUnique</em></div>
<div><span class="br">├─ </span>orm.constraint<span class="br">.*</span><em>unique, notNull, foreignKey, check</em></div>
<div><span class="br">├─ </span>orm.lazy.noSession</div>
<div><span class="br">└─ </span>orm.stale<em>optimistic locking</em></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 6b. OBSERVABILITY -->
<section class="tint">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Observability</span>
      <h2>See every ORM query <span class="grad">with BxLens</span>.</h2>
      <p>BxORM announces each SQL statement, flush and failure as an event. Install <a href="https://bxlens.boxlang.io" style="color:var(--accent)">BxLens</a> and turn on its ORM integration: your ORM SQL shows up next to your other queries, with the time, the rows and the BoxLang line that ran it.</p>
      <ul class="checks">
        <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle"></i><span>ORM SQL in the Queries panel, the Timeline and the console, labelled ORM</span></li>
        <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle"></i><span>The same slow-query and N+1 detection as any other query</span></li>
        <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle"></i><span>Flushes, failures and Hibernate statistics per datasource on the ORM page<span class="badge">BoxLang+</span></span></li>
        <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle"></i><span>Off until you turn it on, and no cost when nothing is listening</span></li>
      </ul>
      <div class="lens-steps">
        <code><span style="color:var(--g1)">$</span> bx-module install bx-lens</code>
        <code>"collectors" : { "orm" : { "enabled" : true } }</code>
        <small>Then open the bar on any page, or the console at <code>/~bxlens/index.bxm</code>. <a href="https://bxlens.boxlang.io/lensbar/orm/" style="color:var(--accent)">ORM in BxLens →</a></small>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="shot">
        <div class="stage-bar"><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span>
          <div class="tabs">
            <button class="on" data-t="lens1">ORM page</button>
            <button data-t="lens2">Queries panel</button>
            <button data-t="lens3">Walkthrough</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div id="lens1"><img data-bxsites-lightbox src="#variables.basePath#assets/bxlens/console-orm.png" alt="The BxLens ORM page: statements, flushes and failures per datasource, and Hibernate statistics"></div>
        <div id="lens2" hidden><img data-bxsites-lightbox src="#variables.basePath#assets/bxlens/queries.png" alt="The BxLens Queries panel with a flagged N+1 group"></div>
        <div id="lens3" hidden><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="https://bxlens.boxlang.io/assets/videos/walkthrough-bar.jpg"><source src="https://bxlens.boxlang.io/assets/videos/walkthrough-bar.mp4" type="video/mp4"></video></div>
        <figcaption>Screens from <a href="https://bxlens.boxlang.io" style="color:var(--accent)">bxlens.boxlang.io</a>. ORM statements appear in the Queries panel the same way, labelled ORM.</figcaption>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 7. BOOT CACHE -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Boot cache</span>
      <h2>Start production without parsing <span class="grad">a single entity</span>.</h2>
      <p>BxORM saves everything it works out at startup in a <code>.bxorm/</code> folder: entity metadata, Hibernate mappings and the generated entity classes. Build it in CI, trust it in production. One setting: <code>ormManifest</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="split" style="align-items:start">
      <div>
        <div class="pipeline">
          <div class="lane"><b><code>"off"</code> every boot</b>
            <div class="steps-h"><span>Discover</span><span>Parse entities</span><span>Generate mappings</span><span>Generate classes</span><span>SessionFactory</span></div></div>
          <div class="lane"><b><code>"auto"</code> development</b>
            <div class="steps-h"><span>Boot normally</span><span class="hot">Write .bxorm/</span><span class="hot">Reload when an entity changes</span></div></div>
          <div class="lane"><b><code>"trust"</code> production</b>
            <div class="steps-h"><span class="skip">Discover</span><span class="skip">Parse</span><span class="skip">Generate</span><span class="hot">Load .bxorm/</span><span>SessionFactory</span></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="ci">
          <span><i class="ph-duotone ph-terminal-window"></i><code>boxlang module:orm generate</code></span><span class="to">→</span>
          <span><i class="ph-duotone ph-folder"></i>.bxorm/</span><span class="to">→</span>
          <span><i class="ph-duotone ph-shipping-container"></i>Docker image</span><span class="to">→</span>
          <span><i class="ph-duotone ph-rocket-launch"></i><code>"trust"</code></span>
        </div>
        <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.86rem;margin-top:14px">The CLI builds the cache with no server, database or application start. A <code>trust</code> boot refuses to start on a stale cache and names what changed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="chart">
        <h3>Median boot time, in seconds</h3>
        <div class="sub">Lower is better</div>
        <div class="grp"><small>250 entities</small>
          <div class="bar"><code>off</code><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:100%"></div></div><b>13.48</b></div>
          <div class="bar"><code>auto</code><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:100%"></div></div><b>14.14</b></div>
          <div class="bar win"><code>trust</code><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:50.4%"></div></div><b>7.12</b></div>
        </div>
        <div class="grp"><small>25 entities</small>
          <div class="bar"><code>off</code><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:37%"></div></div><b>5.23</b></div>
          <div class="bar"><code>auto</code><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:36%"></div></div><b>5.10</b></div>
          <div class="bar win"><code>trust</code><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:27.3%"></div></div><b>3.86</b></div>
        </div>
        <p class="fine">Synthetic models with associations, local MariaDB. From the Performance docs. On a cold class cache a <code>trust</code> boot adds about 2 ms per entity.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 7b. AI SKILLS -->
<section class="tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="eyebrow">AI skills</span>
      <h2>Your coding agent <span class="grad">already knows BxORM</span>.</h2>
      <p>Seven agent skills teach Claude Code, Copilot, Cursor, Codex and friends how BxORM 2 really works: annotations, relationships, criteria, transactions, the boot cache and observability. Install them once and ask in plain words.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="skills"><div class="skill"><code>bx-orm-entities</code><p>Annotations, tables, soft delete, ids and generators, inheritance and static entity methods.</p></div><div class="skill"><code>bx-orm-relationships</code><p>One-to-one to many-to-many, inverse, lazy loading, cascades and the generated add/has/remove methods.</p></div><div class="skill"><code>bx-orm-querying</code><p>The entityLoad family, HQL with ormExecuteQuery(), paging, streaming and the query cache.</p></div><div class="skill"><code>bx-orm-criteria</code><p>entityCriteria(): conditions, joins, subqueries, projections, asStruct() and bulk updates.</p></div><div class="skill"><code>bx-orm-transactions</code><p>transaction{}, mixing ORM and queryExecute(), savepoints, flushing and the session.</p></div><div class="skill"><code>bx-orm-configuration</code><p>ormSettings, dialects, naming strategies, caching, the boot cache and the module:orm CLI.</p></div><div class="skill"><code>bx-orm-observability</code><p>onORMQuery and friends, slow SQL, statistics and ormDiagnostics().</p></div><div class="skill all"><code>+ every BoxLang skill</code><p>Language, modules and frameworks, in one plugin.</p></div></div>
    <div class="howto">
      <div class="stage">
        <div class="stage-bar"><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span>
          <div class="tabs">
            <button class="on" data-t="k4">ColdBox CLI</button>
            <button data-t="k1">npx skills</button>
            <button data-t="k2">Claude Code</button>
            <button data-t="k3">Codex</button>
          </div>
        </div>
<pre class="code" id="k4"><span class="c">## ColdBox app: guidelines, agent files and docs MCP servers</span>
coldbox ai install agent=claude,copilot

<span class="c">## pick the bx-orm-* skills from the registry</span>
coldbox ai skills install --list

<span class="c">## or one by path</span>
coldbox ai skills install ortus-boxlang/skills/boxlang-modules/bx-orm/bx-orm-criteria

<span class="c">## cborm skill (automatic when cborm is in box.json)</span>
coldbox ai skills install coldbox/skills/modules/cborm

<span class="c">## BxORM docs MCP server</span>
coldbox ai mcp add name=bxorm url=https://bxorm.ortusbooks.com/~gitbook/mcp</pre>
<pre class="code" id="k1" hidden><span class="c">## all seven BxORM skills</span>
npx skills add ortus-boxlang/skills/boxlang-modules/bx-orm

<span class="c">## or just one</span>
npx skills add ortus-boxlang/skills/boxlang-modules/bx-orm/bx-orm-criteria</pre>
<pre class="code" id="k2" hidden><span class="c">## every BoxLang skill, plus the BxORM docs MCP server</span>
claude plugin marketplace add ortus-boxlang/skills
claude plugin install boxlang-agent-skills@boxlang-agent-skills</pre>
<pre class="code" id="k3" hidden>codex plugin marketplace add ortus-boxlang/skills
codex plugin add boxlang-agent-skills@boxlang-agent-skills</pre>
      </div>
      <div class="stage">
        <div class="stage-bar"><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="file">Then just ask</span></div>
        <ul class="prompt-list">
          <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-chat-circle-text"></i><span>"Add an Invoice entity with soft delete and a many-to-one to Customer."<em>bx-orm-entities, bx-orm-relationships</em></span></li>
          <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-chat-circle-text"></i><span>"Page the open orders by customer name, 25 at a time, as JSON."<em>bx-orm-criteria</em></span></li>
          <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-chat-circle-text"></i><span>"Build the boot cache in our Dockerfile and trust it in production."<em>bx-orm-configuration</em></span></li>
          <li><i class="ph-duotone ph-chat-circle-text"></i><span>"Why is this page running 40 queries?"<em>bx-orm-observability</em></span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="text-align:center;color:var(--muted);font-size:.86rem;margin-top:18px">Browse them all at <a href="https://skills.boxlang.io" style="color:var(--accent)">skills.boxlang.io</a> · source in <a href="https://github.com/ortus-boxlang/skills" style="color:var(--accent)">ortus-boxlang/skills</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 8. QUICK START -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><span class="eyebrow">Five minutes</span><h2>From empty app to your first entity.</h2><p>The Quick Start, in four steps.</p></div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step-list">
        <button class="step on" data-s="s1"><span class="num">1</span><span><b>Install</b><small>The module and your database driver</small></span></button>
        <button class="step" data-s="s2"><span class="num">2</span><span><b>Configure</b><small>A datasource and <code>ormEnabled</code></small></span></button>
        <button class="step" data-s="s3"><span class="num">3</span><span><b>Model</b><small>A class marked <code>@persistent</code></small></span></button>
        <button class="step" data-s="s4"><span class="num">4</span><span><b>Use it</b><small>Save, load, query, delete</small></span></button>
      </div>
      <div class="step-code">
        <div class="bar2" id="stepname">terminal</div>
<pre class="code" id="s1"><span class="c">## CommandBox</span>
box install bx-orm bx-mysql

<span class="c">## or the BoxLang module installer</span>
bx-module install bx-orm bx-mysql</pre>
<pre class="code" id="s2" hidden><span class="k">class</span> {
    <span class="k">this</span>.name        = <span class="s">"quickstart"</span>;
    <span class="k">this</span>.datasource  = <span class="s">"appDB"</span>;
    <span class="k">this</span>.ormEnabled  = <span class="k">true</span>;
    <span class="k">this</span>.ormSettings = {
        entityPaths   : [ <span class="s">"models"</span> ],
        dbcreate      : <span class="s">"update"</span>,  <span class="c">// development only</span>
        eventHandling : <span class="k">true</span>,
        ormManifest   : <span class="f">getSystemSetting</span>( <span class="s">"ORM_MANIFEST"</span>, <span class="s">"auto"</span> )
    };
}</pre>
<pre class="code" id="s3" hidden><span class="f">@persistent</span>
<span class="f">@table</span>( <span class="s">"users"</span> )
<span class="f">@defaultSort</span>( <span class="s">"lastName"</span> )
<span class="k">class</span> {

    <span class="f">@fieldtype</span>( <span class="s">"id"</span> )
    <span class="f">@generator</span>( <span class="s">"native"</span> )
    <span class="f">@ormtype</span>( <span class="s">"integer"</span> )
    <span class="k">property</span> id;

    <span class="f">@ormtype</span>( <span class="s">"string"</span> )
    <span class="k">property</span> firstName;

    <span class="f">@ormtype</span>( <span class="s">"string"</span> )
    <span class="k">property</span> lastName;

    <span class="k">function</span> <span class="f">getFullName</span>(){
        <span class="k">return</span> <span class="f">getFirstName</span>() &amp; <span class="s">" "</span> &amp; <span class="f">getLastName</span>();
    }
}</pre>
<pre class="code" id="s4" hidden><span class="k">transaction</span> {
    <span class="f">entitySave</span>( <span class="f">entityNew</span>( <span class="s">"User"</span>, { firstName : <span class="s">"Ann"</span>, lastName : <span class="s">"Lee"</span> } ) );
}

lees  = User::<span class="f">findAllWhere</span>( { lastName : <span class="s">"Lee"</span> } );
ann   = User::<span class="f">findWhere</span>( { firstName : <span class="s">"Ann"</span> } );
json  = <span class="f">entityToStruct</span>( ann );

<span class="k">transaction</span> { <span class="f">entityDelete</span>( ann ); }</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 8b. COURSE -->
<section style="padding-top:20px">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><span class="eyebrow">Free course</span><h2>Learn BxORM, <span class="grad">one lesson at a time</span>.</h2><p>Seventeen short lessons: twelve from your first entity to a production boot, then five to go further with inheritance, testing, cborm, AI and moving from CFML. Every lesson ends with code you can run, and your progress is saved in your browser.</p></div>
    <div class="course-head">
      <div class="meta"><span><i class="ph-duotone ph-list-numbers"></i>17 lessons</span><span><i class="ph-duotone ph-clock"></i>About 3 hours</span><span><i class="ph-duotone ph-check-square"></i>Mark lessons complete</span></div>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#variables.basePath#course/01-welcome/">Start lesson 1 <i class="ph-duotone ph-arrow-right"></i></a>
    </div>
    <h3 class="track">The essentials</h3>
    <div class="course"><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/01-welcome/"><span class="n">01</span><span><b>Welcome to BxORM</b><small>What an ORM does, and what BxORM adds on top of Hibernate 7</small></span></a><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/02-install-and-configure/"><span class="n">02</span><span><b>Install and configure</b><small>bx-module install, a datasource, ormSettings, naming</small></span></a><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/03-first-entity/"><span class="n">03</span><span><b>Your first entity</b><small>@persistent, properties, ids, generators and no casting</small></span></a><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/04-save-load-delete/"><span class="n">04</span><span><b>Save, load and delete</b><small>entityNew(), entitySave(), entityLoad() and entityDelete()</small></span></a><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/05-static-helpers/"><span class="n">05</span><span><b>Static helpers</b><small>User::get(), findWhere(), list(), firstOrCreate(), deleteWhere()</small></span></a><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/06-relationships/"><span class="n">06</span><span><b>Relationships</b><small>many-to-one, one-to-many, many-to-many, lazy loading, cascades</small></span></a><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/07-criteria/"><span class="n">07</span><span><b>Criteria queries</b><small>Conditions, automatic joins, projections and paging</small></span></a><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/08-hql-structs-queries/"><span class="n">08</span><span><b>HQL, structs and queries</b><small>ormExecuteQuery(), entityToStruct() and entityToQuery()</small></span></a><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/09-transactions/"><span class="n">09</span><span><b>Transactions and the session</b><small>transaction{}, flushing, dirty checks, locking, ORM with SQL</small></span></a><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/10-events-soft-delete/"><span class="n">10</span><span><b>Events, soft delete, timestamps</b><small>preInsert, postCommit, @softDelete and @autoTimestamp</small></span></a><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/11-errors-observability/"><span class="n">11</span><span><b>Errors and observability</b><small>orm.* errors, ormDiagnostics() and BxLens</small></span></a><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/12-ship-it/"><span class="n">12</span><span><b>Ship it</b><small>The boot cache, the bxorm CLI and the second-level cache</small></span></a></div>
    <h3 class="track">Going further</h3>
    <div class="course"><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/13-inheritance/"><span class="n">13</span><span><b>Inheritance</b><small>@mappedSuperClass, shared base entities, single-table and joined</small></span></a><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/14-testing/"><span class="n">14</span><span><b>Testing ORM code</b><small>A test datasource, a clean session and a transaction per test</small></span></a><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/15-cborm/"><span class="n">15</span><span><b>BxORM with cborm</b><small>BaseORMService, entityService:User injection, ActiveEntity</small></span></a><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/16-building-with-ai/"><span class="n">16</span><span><b>Building with AI</b><small>The seven BxORM skills, the docs MCP server, a feature from a prompt</small></span></a><a class="lesson" href="#variables.basePath#course/17-coming-from-cfml/"><span class="n">17</span><span><b>Coming from CFML</b><small>Moving an existing CFML ORM app: what stays, what changes</small></span></a></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 9. EVERYTHING ELSE -->
<section style="padding-top:20px">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><span class="eyebrow">And the rest</span><h2>Everything else you'd expect. <span class="grad">And some you wouldn't.</span></h2></div>
    <div class="cards"><div class="card"><div class="ico"><i class="ph-duotone ph-trash"></i></div><h3>Soft delete</h3><p><code>@softDelete</code>: deletes mark the row, and every load skips it.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="ico"><i class="ph-duotone ph-clock"></i></div><h3>Automatic timestamps</h3><p><code>@autoTimestamp( "create" )</code> and <code>"update"</code>, set for you.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="ico"><i class="ph-duotone ph-brackets-curly"></i></div><h3>Structs and queries</h3><p><code>entityToStruct()</code> for JSON APIs, mementifier compatible. <code>entityToQuery()</code> for reports.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="ico"><i class="ph-duotone ph-bell-ringing"></i></div><h3>Events with a veto</h3><p>Return <code>false</code> from <code>preInsert</code> to cancel. <code>postCommit</code> only fires for real commits.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="ico"><i class="ph-duotone ph-stack"></i></div><h3>Cache on BoxCache</h3><p>The second-level cache runs on BoxLang caches, distributed ones included.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="ico"><i class="ph-duotone ph-pulse"></i></div><h3>Observability</h3><p><code>onORMQuery</code>, <code>onORMFlush</code> and <code>onORMException</code>, free when nobody listens.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="ico"><i class="ph-duotone ph-lock"></i></div><h3>Locking and read-only</h3><p>Pessimistic locks, optimistic versions and read-only loads.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="ico"><i class="ph-duotone ph-tree-structure"></i></div><h3>Rich models</h3><p>Composite keys, single-table and joined inheritance, value collections.</p></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="padding-top:20px">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><span class="eyebrow">Databases</span><h2>Every database Hibernate supports.</h2></div>
